Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b970d1b6-6afd-4545-8505-abdb05cef706"],

Cell["\<\
1. Tight speed-limit confirmation: In Lab 9A, compare Method -> \"Progressive\
\" against \"Joint\" and \"Hybrid\" at TargetFidelity -> 0.9999. Joint/Hybrid \
hit the continuous limit without fixed-factor overshoot.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cb5cea63-f0ba-2f42-890e-9c87f73ff18f"],

Cell["\<\
2. Bang-bang PMP signature: Inspect PlotSwitchingFunctions for the optimal \
box-constrained inversion pulse: notice u(t) saturates +/-nu_max whenever \
s_x(t) is nonzero and BoundaryFraction equals 1.0.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"07ced89b-3793-2942-b86d-b7c546bc3a2e"],

Cell["\<\
3. Cost of worst-case robustness: In Lab 9B, run Criterion = \"Mean\" vs \
\"Minimum\" at +/-2 kHz. \"Mean\" terminates early with shorter T* while edge \
offsets dip below 0.99, whereas \"Minimum\" guarantees out-of-sample Val(33) \
Min >= 0.99.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2e438594-d9b2-8842-b4d0-67b4994fa089"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e0e8b322-2c76-4945-a79e-e19fc1f07df8"],

Cell["\<\
TimeOptimalControlOptimize, TimeOptimalPulseCurve, \
VerifyOptimalControlStationarity, PlotTimeOptimalPulseCurve, and \
PlotSwitchingFunctions integrate time-optimal pulse searches and local \
Pontryagin diagnostics cleanly with SpinDynamica's GRAPE kernels, \
constraints, and ensembles.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acac0644-faa6-0543-ba6f-575ba98ccfc9"],

